#: main.lua:6998
msgid "Enable Glimpse"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:6999
msgid ""
"Master switch. When off, the bound gesture and the Open Glimpse entry do "
"nothing – a quick way to silence Glimpse without unbinding its gesture."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7013
msgid ""
"Assign or change it under Taps and gestures → Gesture manager → (pick a "
"gesture) → Reader → 'Open Glimpse'."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7017
msgid ""
"Browse the maps, family trees and other reference images found in this book, "
"without losing your reading position. Tip: bind the gesture action 'Open "
"Glimpse' for one-touch access."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7039
msgid ""
"Tip: open Glimpse instantly with a gesture.\n"
"\n"
"Set one under Settings → Taps and gestures → Gesture manager → pick a "
"gesture → Reader → 'Open Glimpse'.\n"
"\n"
"(This tip is shown only once.)"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7050
msgid "Mode: Show all images"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7051
msgid "Mode: Show images up to current chapter"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7054
msgid "Show images up to current chapter"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7055
msgid ""
"Images that appear beyond your current position stay hidden, so you can't "
"spoil yourself. Granularity is per chapter: images in the chapter you are "
"currently reading are shown."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7056
msgid "Show all images"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7057
msgid ""
"Show reference images from anywhere in the book, including parts you haven't "
"reached yet."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7063
msgid "Include Bookmarks in Gallery"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7064
msgid ""
"Also show the pages you've bookmarked (the dogear bookmark) in the Gallery, "
"rendered as page thumbnails and marked with a bookmark badge, in reading "
"order alongside the images – a quick way to keep a reference page a swipe "
"away. Off by default. Also available from the viewer's ⋯ menu (see Quick "
"Actions)."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7075
msgid "Quick Actions"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7076
msgid ""
"Choose which actions appear in the viewer's ⋯ menu. Reset Rotation is "
"automatic (shown while an image is rotated)."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7098
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7101
msgid "Gestures"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7104
msgid "Double-tap for maximum zoom"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7105
msgid ""
"Double-tap the image to jump to the maximum zoom (centered on the tap), and "
"again to return to the fitted view. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7114
msgid "Swipe left/right to navigate"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7115
msgid ""
"Swipe left or right across the image to move to the next or previous image. "
"On by default. (The Gallery's swipe-to-page is unaffected.)"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7124
msgid "Pinch to zoom in/out"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7125
msgid ""
"Pinch or spread two fingers on the image to zoom out or in. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7144
msgid "Layout: %1 · %2"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7146
msgid ""
"Where Glimpse opens: a side panel (left or right) or, in portrait, a band "
"across the top or bottom. In landscape it always uses the preferred side."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7152
msgid "Maximum zoom: %1%"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7155
msgid ""
"How far you can zoom in, as a percentage of the image's own resolution. "
"Double-tap jumps to this level and pinch stops here. Higher reveals more on "
"detailed maps, but past 100% it is upscaling, so very high can look soft."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7162
msgid "%1% (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7163
msgid "%1%"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7177
msgid "Navigation Loops Around"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7178
msgid ""
"Let the ‹ › buttons and swipes wrap around at the ends: Next on the last "
"image goes to the first, and Previous on the first goes to the last. The "
"Gallery pages wrap the same way."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7189
msgid "Show Nav Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7190
msgid ""
"Show ‹ and › buttons in the viewer for switching between images, as an "
"alternative to swiping. A button is grayed out when there is no image on its "
"side."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7200
msgid "Show Zoom Controls"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7201
msgid ""
"Show a vertical −/fit/+ control in the viewer for zooming in and out, as an "
"alternative to double-tap and pinch. The middle button returns to the fitted "
"view."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7211
msgid "Show Mini Map"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7212
msgid ""
"While zoomed in, show a small overview of the image with a rectangle marking "
"the visible area. Tap the map to jump there. It docks to the zoom controls "
"when those are on, and is hidden at the fitted view."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7222
msgid "Invert Images in Night Mode"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7223
msgid ""
"While KOReader's night mode is on, show images inverted (light lines on a "
"dark background). Also toggleable from the viewer's ⋯ menu."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7233
msgid "Show image captions"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7234
msgid ""
"Show the image's caption from the book, overlaid in the viewer's top-left "
"corner."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7243
msgid "Show bookmark label in corner"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7244
msgid ""
"On a bookmarked page, show a label with the page number and chapter in the "
"viewer's top-left corner. Turn off to hide it."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7253
msgid "Numbered indicator instead of dots"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7254
msgid ""
"Show the position as a compact \"3 / 42\" counter instead of a row of dots. "
"Useful when a book has so many images that the dots pill grows very wide. "
"Off by default. (With many images Glimpse switches to the counter on its "
"own; this makes it always so.)"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7266
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7269
msgid "Respect KOReader top menu activation"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7270
msgid ""
"On (default): while the viewer is open, a tap along the top edge opens "
"KOReader's top menu over the drawer, but only when KOReader itself opens its "
"menu on a tap (Settings → Taps and gestures → menu activation includes Tap). "
"Off: Glimpse keeps the top edge for itself, so a top tap never opens the "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7282
msgid "Disable irrelevant image filtering"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7283
msgid ""
"By default Glimpse sets aside covers, publisher logos, ornaments and other "
"non-reference imagery, keeping maps, family trees, diagrams and "
"illustrations. Enable this to switch that off and see every image in the "
"book. (Individual wrongly-kept images can instead be ignored from the "
"viewer's ⋯ menu; wrongly set-aside ones added back from the Gallery's "
"Ignored tab.)"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7294
msgid "Suppress \"format not supported\" notice"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7295
msgid ""
"Silence the message shown when Glimpse is opened on a book format it doesn't "
"support (PDF, comics, manga…). Handy if a reading gesture sometimes triggers "
"Glimpse on non-EPUB files. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7305
msgid "Disable shadows"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7306
msgid ""
"Remove the drawer's drop shadow. The shadow is a dithered gradient – the "
"main cause of e-ink ghosting behind the drawer – so turn it off if a ghost "
"lingers after closing Glimpse. No visible effect on LCD screens."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7316
msgid "Fast image switching"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7317
msgid ""
"Switch between images with a quick, flashless refresh instead of a full "
"clear. On by default: faster and no flash. Turn it off if the previous image "
"ghosts through the next one – most noticeable on detailed maps and on slower "
"e-ink panels. No visible effect on LCD screens."
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7327
msgid "Rescan this book"
msgstr ""

#: main.lua:7328
msgid ""
"Glimpse caches its scan of the book. Use this if the book file was replaced "
"or images seem out of date."
msgstr ""

